## 3. PowerCenter XML Reference (Authoritative)

Tag names, attribute names, and value conventions below come from direct inspection of real customer files. Do not invent variants.

### 3.1 Document skeleton

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE POWERMART SYSTEM "powrmart.dtd">
<POWERMART CREATION_DATE="..." REPOSITORY_VERSION="...">
  <REPOSITORY NAME="..." VERSION="..." CODEPAGE="..." DATABASETYPE="...">
    <FOLDER NAME="..." OWNER="...">
      <MAPPLET .../>           <!-- zero or more; treated as UnknownComponent -->
      <SOURCE .../>
      <TARGET .../>
      <TRANSFORMATION .../>    <!-- FOLDER-level reusable transformations (REUSABLE="YES") -->
      <MAPPING NAME="..." DESCRIPTION="..." ISVALID="YES">
        <TRANSFORMATION .../>  <!-- mapping-local (REUSABLE="NO") -->
        <INSTANCE .../>
        <CONNECTOR .../>
        <TARGETLOADORDER .../>
      </MAPPING>
    </FOLDER>
  </REPOSITORY>
</POWERMART>
```

### 3.2 SOURCE element with FLATFILE config

```xml
<SOURCE NAME="EmployeeMaster" DATABASETYPE="Flat File" DBDNAME="FlatFile">
  <FLATFILE CODEPAGE="MS1252" DELIMITED="YES" DELIMITERS=","
            QUOTE_CHARACTER="DOUBLE" ESCAPE_CHARACTER=""
            NULL_CHARACTER="*" NULLCHARTYPE="ASCII"
            SKIPROWS="1" STRIPTRAILINGBLANKS="NO"
            LINESEQUENTIAL="NO" REPEATABLE="NO"
            CONSECDELIMITERSASONE="NO" MULTIDELIMITERSASAND="YES"/>
  <TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Datetime Format" VALUE="A  19 mm/dd/yyyy hh24:mi:ss"/>
  <SOURCEFIELD NAME="EMPLID_TFS" DATATYPE="string" LENGTH="8" PRECISION="8" SCALE="0"
               NULLABLE="NOTNULL" KEYTYPE="PRIMARY KEY" FIELDNUMBER="1"/>
</SOURCE>
```

**FLATFILE attributes** that land in `dataExtractionRef[].fileConfig`:
- `DELIMITERS` → `delimiter`
- `QUOTE_CHARACTER` (`DOUBLE`/`SINGLE`/`NONE`) → `quoteChar` (`"`/`'`/null)
- `ESCAPE_CHARACTER` → `escapeChar`
- `NULL_CHARACTER` → `nullValue`
- `SKIPROWS` → `skipRows` (int) + derives `hasHeader: true` if > 0
- `STRIPTRAILINGBLANKS` → `stripTrailingBlanks` (bool)
- `CODEPAGE` → `codepage`

**TABLEATTRIBUTE `Datetime Format`** → `dataExtractionRef[].fileConfig.datetimeFormat`, with `mm → MM` correction.

**Per SOURCEFIELD**: `NAME`, `DATATYPE`, `LENGTH`, `PRECISION`, `SCALE`, `NULLABLE` (`NULL`/`NOTNULL`), `KEYTYPE` (`PRIMARY KEY`/`NOT A KEY`), `FIELDNUMBER`, `OFFSET`.

`DATABASETYPE` values: `Flat File`, `Oracle`, `Microsoft SQL Server`, `Snowflake`, `ODBC`. Flat-file sources have `<FLATFILE>` child.

### 3.3 TARGET element

Mirrors SOURCE structurally with `<TARGETFIELD>` children.

### 3.4 TRANSFORMATION element

```xml
<TRANSFORMATION NAME="exp_EMPL_MASTER" TYPE="Expression" REUSABLE="NO">
  <TRANSFORMFIELD NAME="EMPLID" DATATYPE="string" PORTTYPE="INPUT" PRECISION="33"/>
  <TRANSFORMFIELD NAME="Header" DATATYPE="string" PORTTYPE="OUTPUT" PRECISION="500"
                  EXPRESSION="DECODE(TRUE, ISNULL(EMPLID), 'INVALID', EMPLID='EMPLID', 'INVALID', 'VALID')"
                  EXPRESSIONTYPE="GENERAL"
                  DEFAULTVALUE="ERROR('transformation error')"/>
</TRANSFORMATION>
```

**TYPE values + MDDI routing**:

| TYPE | Routing |
|---|---|
| `Source Qualifier` | `dataExtractionRef.sqlQueryRef` if SQL override exists, else pass-through |
| `Filter` | `dataFilteringRef` (with parallel `dataValidationRef` entry if flag pattern detected — Section 8) |
| `Expression` | Per-field split into `calculatedColumnsRef` or `dataMappingRef`; scanned for validation patterns; LOCAL VARIABLE ports become their own calcs |
| `Lookup Procedure` | `lookupRef` |
| `Joiner` | `dataJoinRef` |
| `Router` | `routerRef` (new section, Section 12) |
| `Update Strategy` | `updateStrategyRef` (new section, Section 12) |
| `Aggregator` | `calculatedColumnsRef` with GROUP BY in `extensions` |
| `Sequence` / `Sequence Generator` | `calculatedColumnsRef` (New) with `extensions.sequence_config` |
| `Mapplet` (INSTANCE with `TYPE="MAPPLET"`) | `UnknownComponent` + warning (schema TBD) |
| `Input Transformation` / `Output Transformation` | Skipped at MAPPING level (internal to mapplet definitions) |
| `Sorter` / `Normalizer` / `Rank` / `Union` / `Java` / `SQL` / etc. | `UnknownComponent` + warning |

**TRANSFORMFIELD `PORTTYPE` values**: `INPUT`, `OUTPUT`, `INPUT/OUTPUT`, `VARIABLE`, `LOCAL VARIABLE`, `LOOKUP`, `LOOKUP/OUTPUT`, `RETURN`. LOCAL VARIABLE handled per Section 9.

**Filter condition**: `<TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Filter Condition" VALUE="Header='VALID'"/>`

**Source Qualifier SQL override**: `<TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Sql Query" VALUE="SELECT ..."/>`

**Lookup attributes**:
```xml
<TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Lookup Sql Override"     VALUE="..."/>
<TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Lookup table name"       VALUE="WD_COUNTRY_CODE"/>
<TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Lookup condition"        VALUE="COUNTRY_NAME = HOM_COUNTRY_CODE"/>
<TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Lookup caching enabled"  VALUE="YES"/>
<TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Connection Information"  VALUE="$Target"/>
```

`$Target`, `$Source`, `$PMCacheDir` are PowerCenter session parameters — pass through verbatim into YAML (`connection_ref: $Target`).

**Router**:
```xml
<TRANSFORMATION TYPE="Router" NAME="RTR_CUSTOMER_INS_UPD">
  <GROUP NAME="INPUT"    TYPE="INPUT"/>
  <GROUP NAME="INSERT"   TYPE="OUTPUT"          EXPRESSION="TARGET_FLAG='I'"/>
  <GROUP NAME="UPDATE"   TYPE="OUTPUT"          EXPRESSION="TARGET_FLAG='U'"/>
  <GROUP NAME="DEFAULT1" TYPE="OUTPUT/DEFAULT"/>
</TRANSFORMATION>
```

**Update Strategy**:
```xml
<TRANSFORMATION TYPE="Update Strategy" NAME="UPD_INSERT_CUSTOMER">
  <TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Update Strategy Expression" VALUE="DD_INSERT"/>
</TRANSFORMATION>
```
`DD_INSERT` → `operation: insert`. `DD_UPDATE` → `update`. `DD_DELETE` → `delete`. `DD_REJECT` → `reject`.

**Sequence Generator**:
```xml
<TRANSFORMATION TYPE="Sequence" NAME="SQ_CUSTOMER_KEY" REUSABLE="YES">
  <TRANSFORMFIELD NAME="NEXTVAL" PORTTYPE="OUTPUT"/>
  <TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Start Value"   VALUE="0"/>
  <TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Increment By"  VALUE="1"/>
  <TABLEATTRIBUTE NAME="Current Value" VALUE="15804062"/>
</TRANSFORMATION>
```
→ calculated column with expression `monotonically_increasing_id() + <Current Value>` and full config preserved in `extensions.sequence_config`.

### 3.5 MAPPING / INSTANCE / CONNECTOR

CONNECTORs are the source of truth for dataflow ordering. Collapse all CONNECTORs to unique `(FROMINSTANCE, TOINSTANCE)` edges; topologically sort. Cycles → fatal error.

