## 4. View-Name Resolution

Every node produces an output "view" that downstream nodes reference via `sourceName`:

| Node type | Output view name |
|---|---|
| Source (file `EmployeeMaster.csv`) | `EMPLOYEEMASTER` (strip extension, uppercase) |
| Source (database table `dbo.Customer`) | `CUSTOMER` (strip schema, uppercase) |
| Source Qualifier | upstream source view (pass-through) |
| Filter (`fil_HEADER`) | `FIL_HEADER` (uppercase instance name) |
| Expression (`exp_X`) | upstream view (Expressions modify in-place, no new view) |
| Lookup (with `lookupName: LKP_X`) | `LKP_X` |
| Joiner (`jnr_X`) | `JNR_X` |
| Aggregator (`agg_X`) | `AGG_X` |
| Router (`rtr_X`) | `RTR_X` (single view; group outputs only addressed inside `routerRef`) |
| Update Strategy (`upd_X`) | `UPD_X` |
| Sequence Generator | no view; output port feeds downstream Expression |
| Target | terminus |

