## 5. Architecture — Seven-Phase Pipeline

```
Phase 1: Lossless Parse  (xmltodict → nested dict)

Phase 2: Inventory & Structural Classification
         Walk dict. Map each TRANSFORMATION TYPE via COMPONENT_REGISTRY.
         Build CONNECTOR DAG via networkx. Build view-name map.

Phase 3: Validation Pattern Extraction  (Section 8)
         Scan Expressions for DECODE/IIF flag patterns; pair with
         downstream Filters; decompose into validation rules.

Phase 4: IR Assembly + Expression Translation
         Per-field routing for Expressions. PowerCenter → Spark SQL.
         Auto-derive validation rules from SOURCEFIELD constraints.
         Dedupe XML-origin vs derived rules (XML wins).

Phase 5: Local Variable Resolution  (Section 9)
         LOCAL VARIABLE / VARIABLE ports become own calcs in declaration
         order. Downstream output ports reference them by name.

Phase 6: YAML Generation
         IR → MDDI YAML via Jinja2. Top-level dataFlowExecutionSequence
         is the fixed four-step list; detailed ordering in
         dataTransformationRef.executionSequence.

Phase 7: LLM-as-Judge + Self-Correct  (max MAX_CORRECTION_ROUNDS=3)
```

---

## 6. Filter Intent Classification

| Signal | Intent |
|---|---|
| Filter is downstream of a flag-Expression resolved by Validation Pattern Extraction (Section 8) | `dataFilteringRef` AND parallel `dataValidationRef` entries (BOTH emitted, per meeting decision — round-trip fidelity) |
| Description matches `/(?i)valid\|verify\|check\|quality\|constraint\|invalid\|reject/` AND no flag pattern | `dataValidationRef` only |
| Filter condition is `IS_NULL(pk_col)` / `NOT ISNULL(pk_col)` / `col IS NULL` on PK or NOTNULL column | `dataValidationRef` |
| Otherwise | `dataFilteringRef` |

LLM fallback (`classify_filter_intent`) only when none of the above triggers AND `STRICT_CLASSIFICATION=true`.

