## 7. PowerCenter → Spark SQL Translation

`parser/expression_translator.py`. Lex expressions, walk function-call tree, apply rewrites top-down. **Produce lowercase Spark SQL function names. Use `MM` (not `mm`) for month in date formats.**

| PowerCenter | Spark SQL |
|---|---|
| `IIF(c, t, e)` | `CASE WHEN c THEN t ELSE e END` |
| `IIF(c, t)` | `CASE WHEN c THEN t ELSE NULL END` |
| `DECODE(x, v1, r1, v2, r2, …, default)` | `CASE WHEN x = v1 THEN r1 WHEN x = v2 THEN r2 … ELSE default END` |
| `DECODE(TRUE, c1, r1, c2, r2, …, default)` | `CASE WHEN c1 THEN r1 WHEN c2 THEN r2 … ELSE default END` |
| `ISNULL(x)` / `IS_NULL(x)` | `x IS NULL` |
| `NOT ISNULL(x)` / `NOT IS_NULL(x)` | `x IS NOT NULL` |
| `NVL(x, y)` | `COALESCE(x, y)` |
| `LTRIM(RTRIM(x))` / `RTRIM(LTRIM(x))` | `trim(x)` |
| `LTRIM(x)` / `RTRIM(x)` | `ltrim(x)` / `rtrim(x)` |
| `UPPER(x)` / `LOWER(x)` / `INITCAP(x)` | `upper(x)` / `lower(x)` / `initcap(x)` |
| `SUBSTR(x, start, len)` | `substring(x, start, len)` |
| `INSTR(s, sub)` | `position(sub in s)` |
| `LENGTH(x)` | `length(x)` |
| `CONCAT(a, b)` / `a \|\| b` | `concat(a, b)` |
| `TO_CHAR(d, 'yyyy/mm/dd')` | `date_format(d, 'yyyy/MM/dd')` |
| `TO_DATE(s, 'yyyy/mm/dd')` | `to_date(s, 'yyyy/MM/dd')` |
| `TO_INTEGER(x)` | `CAST(x AS INT)` |
| `TO_DECIMAL(x, p)` | `CAST(x AS DECIMAL(38, p))` |
| `TO_NUMBER(x)` | `CAST(x AS NUMERIC)` |
| `SYSDATE` / `SYSTIMESTAMP` | `current_timestamp()` |
| `ABS(x)` / `ROUND(x, n)` / `MOD(a, b)` | identical, lowercased |
| `ERROR('msg')` | Preserve in `extensions.on_error="raise"` |
| `DD_INSERT` / `DD_UPDATE` / `DD_DELETE` / `DD_REJECT` | Handled at Update Strategy level (Section 12) |

**Date format normalization**: any literal containing `mm/dd`, `dd/mm`, `mm-dd` inside a date function → `mm → MM`. Pre-existing `MM`, `mi`, `MI` left alone.

Functions not in this table → `LLM.translate_expression` fallback. Original PowerCenter expression always preserved on the IR node as `original_expression`.

