## 13. MDDI YAML Output Rules

Match the reference samples exactly, especially `tests/fixtures/golden/employee_master.yaml`.

### 13.1 Top-level structure

```yaml
metadataConfig:
  label: <MAPPING NAME>
  isActive: true
  isAuditEnabled: true
  audit: ''
  versionHistory:
    - changedOn: '<YYYY-MM-DD>'           # from POWERMART CREATION_DATE
    - changedBy: <repository owner>
    - changeDescription: <MAPPING DESCRIPTION>
    - changeApprovedBy: ''

  sourceMetadataRef: [...]
  targetMetadataRef: [...]
  dataExtractionRef: [...]
  dataValidationRef: { isActive: true, rules: [...] }
  dataTransformationRef:
    dataJoinRef:          { isActive: <bool>, joins: [...] }
    dataFilteringRef:     { isActive: <bool>, filters: [...] }
    calculatedColumnsRef: { isActive: <bool>, columns: [...] }
    lookupRef:            { isActive: <bool>, lookups: [...] }
    routerRef:            { isActive: <bool>, items: [...] }
    updateStrategyRef:    { isActive: <bool>, items: [...] }
    executionSequence: [...]
  dataLoadRef: [...]
  dataMappingRef: [...]

  dataFlowExecutionSequence:
    - DataExtraction
    - DataValidation
    - DataTransformation
    - DataLoad
```

Top-level `dataFlowExecutionSequence` is always the four-step fixed order. Include `DataValidation` only if rules exist. Include `DataTransformation` only if any sub-block is active. Always include `DataExtraction` and `DataLoad`.

### 13.2 sourceMetadataRef / targetMetadataRef

- `numberOfAttributes` = count of `attributes`.
- Attributes listed in `FIELDNUMBER` order (sources) / `attributePosition` order (targets).
- `attributeType` normalized: `string`, `integer`, `number`, `decimal`, `timestamp`, `date`. Map: `string|nstring` → `string`, `integer|small integer|bigint` → `integer`, `decimal|double|real` → `decimal`, `date/time` → `timestamp`.
- `nullable: false` when `NULLABLE="NOTNULL"`.

### 13.3 dataExtractionRef

```yaml
dataExtractionRef:
  - dataSourceType: File
    dataSourceFilePath: ''
    dataSourceName: EmployeeMaster.csv
    fileConfig:
      delimiter: ','
      quoteChar: '"'
      escapeChar: ''
      nullValue: '*'
      skipRows: 1
      hasHeader: true
      stripTrailingBlanks: false
      codepage: MS1252
      datetimeFormat: 'MM/dd/yyyy HH:mm:ss'
    sqlQueryRef:
      isActive: false
```

For database sources: `dataSourceType: Database`, add `databaseType: <ORACLE|MSSQL|SNOWFLAKE|POSTGRES>` and `connection_ref` (passes through `$Source` etc.).

### 13.4 dataValidationRef

```yaml
dataValidationRef:
  isActive: true
  rules:
    - sourceName: EMPLOYEEMASTER
      checkType: ROW_COUNT
      column: ''
      minRows: 1
      severity: ERROR
    - sourceName: EMPLOYEEMASTER
      checkType: NOT_NULL
      column: EMPLID_TFS
      severity: ERROR
    - sourceName: EMPLOYEEMASTER
      checkType: NOT_NULL
      column: EMPLID
      severity: ERROR
    - sourceName: EMPLOYEEMASTER
      checkType: CUSTOM
      column: EMPLID
      parameters:
        expression: "EMPLID <> 'EMPLID'"
      severity: ERROR
```

Omit the entire block when no rules exist. `origin` and `xml_source`/`derivation_reason` are NOT emitted in the YAML (they live in the IR/audit only).

### 13.5 dataTransformationRef

```yaml
dataTransformationRef:
  dataJoinRef:
    isActive: <bool>
    joins:
      - id: 1
        joinObjectName: <JOIN_RESULT>
        sourceName: ["<UPSTREAM_A>", "<UPSTREAM_B>"]
        joinType: left
        joinCriteria: "<spark sql condition>"
        filterCriteria: ''
        returnAttributes: [...]

  dataFilteringRef:
    isActive: <bool>
    filters:
      - id: 1
        filterName: FIL_HEADER
        sourceName: EMPLOYEEMASTER
        filterCriteria: "HEADER = 'VALID'"

  calculatedColumnsRef:
    isActive: <bool>
    columns:
      - id: 1
        sourceName: EMPLOYEEMASTER
        columnName: HEADER
        columnCategory: New                    # New | Replace
        dataType: string
        expression: |-
          CASE
            WHEN EMPLID IS NULL    THEN 'INVALID'
            WHEN EMPLID = 'EMPLID' THEN 'INVALID'
            ELSE 'VALID'
          END

  lookupRef:
    isActive: <bool>
    lookups:
      - id: 1
        lookupName: LKP_HOM_COUNTRY
        sourceName: FIL_HEADER
        lookupObjectName: WD_COUNTRY_CODE
        dataSourceType: Database
        connection_ref: $Target
        joinType: left
        joinCriteria: "COUNTRY_NAME = HOM_COUNTRY_CODE"
        returnColumns:
          - fromColumn: ISO_ALPHA3
            asColumn: HOM_COUNTRY_CODE
        cacheEnabled: true

  routerRef:
    isActive: <bool>
    items: [...]               # see Section 12.1

  updateStrategyRef:
    isActive: <bool>
    items: [...]               # see Section 12.2

  executionSequence: [...]     # see Section 12.3
```

Lookup chaining via `sourceName`: lookup 2 with `sourceName: LKP_HOM_COUNTRY` chains off lookup 1's output.

### 13.6 dataLoadRef

For File targets:
```yaml
dataLoadRef:
  - dataLoadTableName: <TARGET_NAME>
    dataLoadType: File
    dataLoadFileType: csv
    dataLoadFolder: ''
    dataMappingTableName: <TARGET_NAME>
    dataSourceName: <last upstream view name>
    writeMode: overwrite
```

For Database targets:
```yaml
dataLoadRef:
  - dataLoadTableName: WD_EMPL_MASTER
    dataLoadType: Database
    connection_ref: $Target
    writeMode: overwrite
    dataSourceName: LKP_LOC_COUNTRY
    dataMappingTableName: WD_EMPL_MASTER
    databaseType: MSSQL
    dataLoadSchema: dbo
```

**Full set of `writeMode` values**: `insert`, `append`, `overwrite`, `update`, `upsert`, `truncate-and-insert`.

How to choose:
- No Update Strategy upstream → `overwrite` (matches `test.yml`)
- Single Update Strategy upstream with DD_INSERT → `insert`
- Single Update Strategy with DD_UPDATE → `update`
- Multiple Update Strategies (Router → INSERT+UPDATE pattern) → emit one `dataLoadRef` per target, each pointing to its respective Update Strategy via `dataSourceName`

`dataSourceName` is the output view of the **last transformation INSTANCE** in topological order before the target.

### 13.7 dataMappingRef

```yaml
dataMappingRef:
  - targetTableName: WD_EMPL_MASTER
    attributes:
      - sourceAttributeName: EMPLID
        targetAttributeName: EMPLID
      - sourceAttributeName: PERSON_CLASS
        targetAttributeName: EMPL_CLASS         # rename
```

Built from CONNECTORs whose `TOINSTANCETYPE="Target Definition"`. Target fields with no incoming CONNECTOR are omitted.

### 13.8 YAML style

- **Block style only.** Never use flow style (`{key: val}`).
- 2-space indent.
- Single-quote strings unless they contain single quotes.
- Multi-line expressions use `|-` literal block scalar.
- No anchors, no aliases.

