## 14. LLM-as-Judge Rubric

`judge/rubric.py`. Mostly deterministic with LLM for semantic checks.

| # | Check | Type |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | YAML valid against MDDI JSON Schema | deterministic |
| 2 | Every `<SOURCE>` appears in `sourceMetadataRef`; `numberOfAttributes` matches | deterministic |
| 3 | Every `<TARGET>` appears in `targetMetadataRef` | deterministic |
| 4 | Every `<TRANSFORMATION>` instance contributes to the IR (or is `UnknownComponent`) | deterministic |
| 5 | Every CONNECTOR feeding a target appears in `dataMappingRef` | deterministic |
| 6 | All `expression:` values are valid Spark SQL (no `IIF`/`DECODE`/`ISNULL`/`DD_*` leakage; no lowercase `mm` in date formats) | regex + LLM |
| 7 | `dataTransformationRef.executionSequence` is a topological order of the CONNECTOR DAG | deterministic |
| 8 | Every calc's `sourceName` references a valid upstream view in `view_name_map` | deterministic |
| 9 | Every `lookupRef.sourceName` references upstream view or prior lookup | deterministic |
| 10 | `dataLoadRef.dataSourceName` references the last view in the topological chain | deterministic |
| 11 | `numberOfAttributes` matches `len(attributes)` for every schema | deterministic |
| 12 | Top-level `dataFlowExecutionSequence` is the four canonical step names in canonical order | deterministic |
| 13 | All validation rules have either `origin: xml` audit trail or `derivation_reason` audit trail | deterministic (IR check) |
| 14 | Every router output group referenced by an `updateStrategyRef.routerGroup` exists | deterministic |
| 15 | XML-extracted validation rules deduped correctly against auto-derived | deterministic |

Failed items → structured errors → `correct_yaml`. Max `MAX_CORRECTION_ROUNDS=3`.

